mode: "100644"
text: "# Educational + how-to content 2026 — verified\n\n*Teaching principles are durable; format metrics + algorithm weights shift. Re-verify quarterly. (Stats are\ncited marketing-research claims — attribute, don't present as hard fact.)*\n\n## The POV: teach one thing completely, accurately\nTeaching is the **highest-trust, highest-save authority builder.** **Saves + sends are top-weighted 2026\nsignals** (Mosseri's confirmed top Instagram signals are watch time, likes per reach, and **sends per reach** —\nand 2026 updates weight DM shares, saves, watch time + profile clicks far above raw likes) and\n**educational/how-to content is the most reliable way to earn them** — it's naturally **reference-worthy.** The win isn't recycled generic\ntips (\"the same 'save this' CTAs everyone posts\") — it's **one genuinely useful idea, taught completely and\naccurately.** \"Give value upfront; the audience returns it with attention, saves, and intent.\" Be a **visual\nteacher: solve a problem, don't sell.**\n\n## Why educational wins (cited — attribute)\nCarousels (educational content's most-saved home) show the **highest save rate (~3× Reels)**, highest\nengagement (~**0.55%** vs ~0.50% Reels vs ~0.41% static — Socialinsider, 31M posts), **longest lifespan**, and\nbest **authority-building** (Buffer/CreatorsJet 2026). **Tutorials are \"inherently saveable\"** + high\ncompletion (a numbered sequence pulls swipes to the end). A teaching carousel delivers **25–40× the dwell time**\nof a static image.\n\n## The teaching unit: \"one job well\"\nTeach **one process, prove one point, or move toward one next step.** **\"Each slide/unit is a flashcard, not a\nchapter\"** — exactly one idea, clearly expressed. **Don't cram two steps into one unit.** Consistent layout so\nthe sequence feels smooth.\n\n## Structure + frameworks\n- **Hook/cover** (answers \"is this for me?\" + \"what will I get?\" — a specific number/outcome, <8–10 words) →\n  **context** (the problem/stakes; proof or specificity by unit 2) → **value** (one step/idea per unit) →\n  **recap** (summary unit) → **CTA** (specific). Structures: **step-by-step** (process), **PAS**\n  (problem-agitate-solve), **myth-busting**, **data-driven.** AIDA across the arc.\n- **Length:** **8–12 units** for most educational; **12–20** for deep guides/teardowns/case studies. **Every\n  unit earns its place** — don't pad (padding buries the idea + kills completion).\n\n## The angle works across formats (route to the writer)\n**Carousel** (the save king — IG + LinkedIn document posts; B2B \"visual teacher\" frameworks à la Welsh/Bloom) ·\n**tutorial/how-to video** (Reel/TikTok/Short — step-by-step screen or talking-head; \"things I wish I knew\") ·\n**thread** (X/Threads — numbered teaching) · **how-to post/blog.** Same lesson, different format.\n\n## CTAs, serialize + evergreen\nTeaching CTAs: **\"save this for later\"** (save), **\"send to the person who handles X\"** (share), **\"comment\nGUIDE and I'll send the full checklist\"** (lead-gen → `lead-magnets-and-funnels`/`social-selling-and-dm`). Soft\nCTA mid + clear CTA at the end. **Serialize** a recognizable weekly series (compounds authority); educational\ncontent is **evergreen** (\"a saved post keeps producing value weeks later\") → repurpose one lesson across\nformats (`content-recycling`); one blog → a 10-unit lesson. **Measure saves/sends, not likes.**\n\n## The accuracy gate (non-negotiable)\n**Teaching wrong information destroys authority + trust.** **Cite sources** for stats/claims; **stay within\ngenuine expertise.** For **YMYL** topics (health, finance, legal, safety) inaccurate how-to content can cause\n**real harm** — add a **\"not professional advice\" disclaimer**, point to a qualified professional, and take\nextra care. **Never fabricate steps or stats.**\n"
